We apply the exact same ratio estimator formulation, though mathematically, the cluster total $t_i$ is now an *estimated* total $\hat{t}_i$. We will display the summary using `gt`'s interactive pagination.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
coots_res <- cluster_ratio_est(data = coots, 
                               cname = "clutch", 
                               csize = "csize", 
                               yvar = "volume")

coots_res$summary |> 
  gt() |> 
  tab_header(title = "Cluster-Level Summary (Coots)") |>
  cols_label(
    Cluster = md("**Clutch**"),
    Mi = md("$M_i$"),
    ybari = md("$\\bar{y}_i$"),
    ti_hat = md("$\\hat{t}_i$")
  ) |> 
  fmt_number(columns = c(ybari, ti_hat), decimals = 2) |> 
  tab_options(
    container.height = px(400),   # Restricts table height
    container.overflow.y = TRUE   # Enables the vertical scroll bar
  )
```

